.TH 1989 1 "October 2026" "1989 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
1989 \- NeXT (Motorola 68030/68040) emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 1989
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 1989
is a work-in-progress emulator of the NeXT family of Motorola 68K based
workstations (NeXT Computer, NeXTcube, NeXTcube Turbo, NeXTstation and
NeXTstation Color, plus the optional NeXTdimension graphics board). It is
built on the "Previous" NeXT emulator code base: the m68k core comes from
WinUAE, and the i860 NeXTdimension emulation from Jason Eckhardt, all
rendered through an SDL3 desktop interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show brief command-line help and exit.
.PP
All machine configuration (machine type, RAM, ROM paths, disk images,
networking, sound, screen mode, shortcut keys) is stored in the per-user
configuration file and edited through the SDL options dialog, opened with
\fBF12\fR (or \fBAlt+O\fR).
.SH KEYS
1989 follows the shared "happy years" conventions: an F9 options overlay, an
activity LED bar at the bottom of the window, and dedicated F-keys.
.PP
Default shortcut keys:
.TP
.B F1
Open the legacy options dialog (kept until every option is migrated to the
F9 overlay).
.TP
.B F4
Save a screenshot (PPM).
.TP
.B F5
Reset the emulated machine.
.TP
.B F6
Toggle GIF capture.
.TP
.B F9
Open / close the options overlay (General, Media, Extensions and - with
Tinker on - Advanced tabs).
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B F12
Quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl++
Increase the window scale.
.TP
.B Ctrl+-
Decrease the window scale.
.TP
.B Alt+O / Alt+F / Alt+M / Alt+C / Alt+G / Alt+R
Options dialog / fullscreen / mouse grab / cold reset / screenshot / sound
recording.
.TP
.B Alt+P / Alt+D / Alt+I / Alt+B / Alt+T
Pause / m68k debugger / i860 debugger / status bar / title bar.
.PP
While the overlay is open, use Left/Right to switch tabs, Up/Down to select
a row, Enter to toggle or choose, and Esc or F9 to close (settings are
saved).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/1989/1989.conf
Main configuration file, created with defaults on first run and written by
the options overlay / dialog. A legacy
.I ~/.previous
directory is used if the new one is absent.
.TP
.I ~/.config/1989/
Default directory for screenshots and recordings.
.TP
.I $pkgdatadir/roms
Install-time location of the NeXT firmware images (see
.I ROMS.md
).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL3 (3)
.SH BUGS
This is scaffolding work based on the upstream "Previous" 4.3 emulator.
See DEVELOPMENT.md for the integration status and roadmap.